Z||000025||Songman||05-11-2001||01:24 AM||||Is this an all Fiero event or what? Is it worth an 11 hour drive from Nashville? What about recommendations for places to stay up there?<P>Would love to meet all of you up there!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||RossT||05-11-2001||02:12 AM||||song.. it is an all fiero event.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierokid/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierokid/</A> <P>last year they had 140+ cars. 4 days of nothing but fiero fun.  The hotel is cool, with a tower overlooking the car show.  Old Lar drives all the way from New York. Lots of non fiero things to do too.  The Dells is a great tourist town, with the world largest water park etc...<P>Lots of fun!!||||reg||1
Z||000027||RossT||05-11-2001||02:50 AM||||Speaking of "Old Lar"... You probably attend more fiero shows than anyone else..  You would do all of us a great service if you rank the shows or tell us whats unique about each one!!  Some of us have to pic and choose the shows, and it would be nice to know what each show has to offer!!||||reg||1
Z||000028||Old Lar||05-11-2001||08:09 AM||||Its really hard to rank the shows. I started going to Fiero shows because I had a Fiero and wanted some place to drive to and to see different parts of the country.  Daytona is a nice show, because it gets me away from a long upstate winter.  It's nice because there are lots of Fieros and lots of other cars to look at.  The Dells is nice, I had never been to Wisconsin prior to the Dells show and there are some of the most enthusiastic Fiero sponsors putting the show on. Nice resort hotel.  The Carlisle show is close by and there are also lots of other cars around to check out. (Weather seems to suck for this show).  The FOCOA national is all over the place so I get to see new places and lots of Fieros.  The FOCONE shows are up in New England,Old Orchard Beach, LLBeans in Freeport, I have friends in Maine so get to see them, the fall show, I go cross country through the Green Mountain National Park and see some real nice scenic views. Plus a trip down to Bob Parker's Kick Hill Farms. There are many shows I haven't gotten to. I still have to work and there is only so much vacation time.<P>Mostly I just use the Fieros on road trips.||||reg||6
Z||000029||Songman||05-11-2001||09:51 PM||||How much can I expect to spend to stay up there? Sorry for all the questions. Just trying to work out the logisitics..and the budget!<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000030||RossT||05-12-2001||12:00 AM||||Song, The hotel runs about $90 a night, but it is well worth it! They have 4 pools etc.<BR>You would be best to try and room with someone else.  I know that David Gunsel was looking to slpit the costs with someone.  Maybee post a message later about rooming with someone.  Archie has several rooms booked too.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000031||FieroMaster88||05-12-2001||12:26 AM||||I will probably go....just hope to get all this mess with my car worked out by then....well, i hope it is worked out before carlisle, i got 5 more days<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
